{{also|Henna|hénna|henną}}

==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ar|حِنَّاء}}, the name of the tree used to make the dye, probably from {{der|en|pal||tr=*hannāy-||to smear, anoint}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hɛnə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-henna.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛnə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[shrub]], {{taxfmt|Lawsonia inermis|species}}, having fragrant reddish flowers
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} A reddish [[plant]] substance, prepared from the dried leaves of this plant, used for temporary [[tattoo]]s and [[hair]] coloring. Hair colorings range from bright red to earth brown to near black.
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} A rich [[red]]dish-[[brown]] colour.
#: {{color panel|882D17}}

